        "original_id": "35036be2-3e79-5629-acac-49a4ff7198c6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Björn Ulvaeus, Agnetha Fältskog, Benny Andersson, Anni-Frid Lyngstad\n- Organizations: ABBA\n- Places: Stockholm, Sweden\n- Roles: songwriter, producer, co-composer\n- Products: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Topics: Swedish pop music, musicals, film production\n\nFacts:\n- Björn Ulvaeus was born on 25 April 1945.\n- ABBA was a Swedish pop group formed in Stockholm in 1972 by Agnetha Fältskog, Björn Ulvaeus, Benny Andersson, and Anni-Frid Lyngstad.\n- Björn Ulvaeus was a member of ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Björn Ulvaeus is a Swedish songwriter and producer who was also credited as Björn Ulvæus.\n- Björn Ulvaeus co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- Björn Ulvaeus co-produced the film \"Mamma Mia!\" with fellow ABBA member Benny Andersson.",
